{"units":[
{"id":"tsdb/block.go:(*BlockMetaCompaction).SetSelectedSeries","summary":"Adds a method that appends the from-selected-series hint to block meta if absent and keeps hints sorted. It is idempotent and persisted in meta.json.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Add SetSelectedSeries to record from-selected-series compaction hint","confidence":0.7,"reason":"Writes a new value into persisted block meta hints, which other code uses to decide WAL-replay cutoff.","risk_signals":["persisted format"],"focus":["Hint string and sorted order are stable in meta.json for older readers"]},
{"id":"tsdb/block.go:(*BlockMetaCompaction).FromSelectedSeries","summary":"Adds a read-only predicate checking whether the hints contain from-selected-series. It is used by planning, merging and the in-order max time computation.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Add FromSelectedSeries hint predicate","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Simple side-effect-free lookup; the risky behavior is in its callers, which are reviewed separately.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/block_test.go:TestBlockMetaCompaction_SetSelectedSeries","summary":"New unit test covering absence, set, idempotence and coexistence with the stale hint. Test-only.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Test selected-series hint set/get idempotence","confidence":0.95,"reason":"New test only; cannot affect production behavior.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/compact.go:(*LeveledCompactor).plan","summary":"The planner now splits blocks into stale, selected and no-hint classes and plans each separately, preferring no-hint, then stale, then selected. This keeps partial-view hints from being lost by mixing, which would advance the WAL-replay cutoff.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Planner segregates selected-series blocks from other compaction classes","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Changes which blocks get compacted together, affecting persisted data and WAL-replay data-loss protection.","risk_signals":["compaction planning","data loss protection"],"focus":["Class ordering cannot starve stale or selected blocks indefinitely","Single-class case still goes through planClass(dms) unchanged","Overlapping blocks of different classes stay unmerged on disk until retention"]},
{"id":"tsdb/compact.go:(*LeveledCompactor).planClass","summary":"Only the doc comment is updated to mention the selected-series hint.","issues":[],"bucket":"none","change_kind":"docs","headline":"Update planClass doc comment for selected-series hint","confidence":0.97,"reason":"Comment-only change; no code lines are modified.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/compact.go:CompactBlockMetas","summary":"Merged block meta now keeps the from-selected-series hint when any source has it, and comments are updated. Combined with planner segregation this preserves the hint through compaction.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Merged block meta propagates from-selected-series hint","confidence":0.88,"reason":"Changes persisted hint output of compaction, which feeds inOrderBlocksMaxTime and WAL truncation.","risk_signals":["persisted format","data loss protection"],"focus":["Any-source semantics are safe given the planner segregation","Hint is dropped nowhere else when merging"]},
{"id":"tsdb/compact.go:(*LeveledCompactor).Write","summary":"Write now copies the from-selected-series hint from the base meta to the new block meta, like the stale hint. This preserves the hint when rewriting a block.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Write propagates from-selected-series hint from base meta","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Alters persisted block meta of written blocks, affecting WAL-replay cutoff logic.","risk_signals":["persisted format"],"focus":["Other Write callers passing a base meta get the intended hint behavior"]},
{"id":"tsdb/db_test.go:TestCompactSelectedSeries","summary":"New happy-path test for CompactSelectedSeries checking eviction, hint, HeadMinTime and metrics. Test-only.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Add happy-path test for CompactSelectedSeries","confidence":0.92,"reason":"New test only; no production code is affected.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]}
]}

{"units":[
{"id":"tsdb/compact_test.go:BenchmarkFilterSeriesAndSortPostings","summary":"Adds a benchmark of Head.filterSeriesAndSortPostings at several input fractions. It is test-only and never runs in production, so a short skim is enough.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"New benchmark for filterSeriesAndSortPostings across input sizes","confidence":0.95,"reason":"New benchmark in a _test.go file; cannot affect production behavior.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/db.go:var compactHeadViewBeforeEvictTestingCallback","summary":"Adds a package-level test hook variable that is nil by default. It is invoked by compactHeadViewLocked before eviction and lets tests inject appends.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Adds test-only callback hook before series eviction","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Nil-by-default testing hook; only tests set it, so production behavior is unchanged.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/db.go:(*DB).compactHeadViewLocked","summary":"Extracts the block-write and evict loop shared by stale-head and selected-series compaction. It adds an appendID watermark captured before the write, so series that received later samples are not evicted. The loop bound is now inclusive and empty writes are skipped. This decides which series are dropped from the head and tombstoned in the WAL, so data loss is possible if it is wrong.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Shared head-view compaction with append-ID watermark guarding eviction","confidence":0.9,"reason":"Persistence and eviction logic with concurrency semantics and a changed loop bound; wrong behavior can lose samples.","risk_signals":["persistence","concurrency","data loss on eviction","loop bound changed"],"focus":["committedAppendID is captured before any block write and is the right watermark when isolation is on","behavior when isolation is disabled: the watermark is 0 and the guard is a no-op","inclusive mint <= maxt loop together with the skip on empty uids does not leave blocks overlapping evicted data","the testing callback global is reset after one use"]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:(*Head).selectedSeriesIndex","summary":"Renames staleIndex to selectedSeriesIndex and switches it to the renamed reader and ref types. The body is otherwise identical.","issues":[],"bucket":"none","change_kind":"rename","headline":"Rename staleIndex to selectedSeriesIndex","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Pure rename of an unexported method and its types with the body unchanged; the callers shown (SelectedSeriesHead.Index) are updated.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:type headSelectedSeriesIndexReader","summary":"Renames headStaleIndexReader to headSelectedSeriesIndexReader, renames its field, and updates the doc comment. The struct layout is unchanged.","issues":[],"bucket":"none","change_kind":"rename","headline":"Rename headStaleIndexReader to headSelectedSeriesIndexReader","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Rename of an unexported type and field with the same layout; the PR updates its uses.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:type seriesRefs","summary":"Renames the unexported struct staleSeriesRefs to seriesRefs with identical fields.","issues":[],"bucket":"none","change_kind":"rename","headline":"Rename staleSeriesRefs to seriesRefs","confidence":0.88,"reason":"Pure rename of an unexported struct with identical fields; all uses are updated in the PR.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:(*Head).filterSeriesAndSortPostings","summary":"Generalizes the stale-series ref collection into a filter taking arbitrary postings and a keep predicate. The predicate runs under the series lock, and a nil predicate accepts every series. The stale-specific logic moves to staleSeriesRefsNoOOOData, and the debug log text changes. The old headStaleIndexReader.SortedPostings is removed from this unit; the replacement is in the not-shown headSelectedSeriesIndexReader.SortedPostings.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"refactor","headline":"Generalize stale-series filtering into predicate-based filterSeriesAndSortPostings","confidence":0.8,"reason":"New shared filtering used to pick which series get evicted; the locking and sorting behavior must match the old stale path.","risk_signals":["concurrency (series lock)","used for selecting evicted series"],"focus":["the lock is held only around keep and not during the sort","sortedByRef keeps input order and sortedByLabels stays label-sorted for the index reader","the removed SortedPostings override is replaced by the renamed reader","unresolved refs are dropped and do not produce an error"]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:(*Head).staleSeriesRefsNoOOOData","summary":"Re-implements staleSeriesRefsNoOOOData on top of filterSeriesAndSortPostings using the shared predicates isSeriesWithoutOOO and isStaleSeries. The predicate matches the old inline OOO and stale-NaN checks.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"refactor","headline":"Stale ref collection now delegates to generic filter","confidence":0.8,"reason":"Refactor with an equivalent predicate (no OOO and stale last value) evaluated under the series lock as before.","risk_signals":[],"focus":[]}
]}
